**How to implement.** The Data locations window, single-instance in the host registry (001 §G; .spec-md §4: every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`; Materials and Library are single-instance through the same registry, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:182`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Data locations group (step 193): `dataLocationsWindow` (`"DataLocationsWindow"`) with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs`: `WindowKey` (`WindowLauncher.fs:34`) gains `DataLocationsWindowKey`, documented in one line: the single-instance Data locations window. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `KitStartWindow.fs` (step 179): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type DataLocationsWindow(locations : DataLocations, explorer : ExplorerProxy)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `KitStartWindow` does; its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §G and spec 0050 S5.3. Its title is `Data locations`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.dataLocationsWindow`; it asks for 720 × 460 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`); it runs `Program.mkSimple` over `initDataLocations { locations = locations; explorer = explorer }`, `updateDataLocations` and `dataLocationsView` (step 193). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `rootWindowFactory` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:44`) answers `DataLocationsWindowKey` with `DataLocationsWindow(TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName "WireUiFinalCompositionTests"), ExplorerProxy.createInMemory ignore)`, and `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff` adds `DataLocationsWindowKey` to the keys it opens, so ui-smoke renders the window. (5) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the Data locations window leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "DataLocations"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `DataLocationsWindow` over `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName "ScrollExtentTests")` and `ExplorerProxy.createInMemory ignore`. `DataLocationsWindowTests` (step 193) gains, without a trait, `the Data locations window is titled and carries its stable id`: the window is titled `Data locations` and carries `dataLocationsWindow` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`; and, with trait `ui-smoke`, `the Data locations window opens once through the registry`: two `openOrActivate DataLocationsWindowKey` through `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory building the window answer `CreatedWindow` and then `ActivatedWindow` of the same window, which is then closed.

**Acceptance.** After the window lands, `DataLocationsWindow` MUST run the Data locations screen titled `Data locations`, fitted to its screen and single-instance under `DataLocationsWindowKey`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Data locations window opens once through the registry` and the widened `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data locations window is titled and carries its stable id` and `the Data locations window leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
